## Why This Is Asked

Tests for idempotent APIs are critical in distributed systems to prevent duplicate side effects, especially with downstream payment and warehouse services.

## Key Concepts

- Idempotency keys and deduplication
- Retry semantics and backoff strategies
- End-to-end vs component-level contracts
- Data isolation across clients

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example Express snippet demonstrating idempotency handling
const orders = new Map();
app.post('/orders', async (req, res) => {
  const key = req.headers['idempotency-key'];
  if (!key) return res.status(400).send({error:'Idempotency-Key required'});
  if (orders.has(key)) return res.json({ orderId: orders.get(key).orderId, cached:true });
  const orderId = generateOrderId();
  // simulate payment call etc.
  orders.set(key, { orderId });
  res.json({ orderId });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test that a retry after a 5xx does not generate a new order with a different id?
- How would you structure tests to verify idempotency across multiple services (gateway, payment, warehouse)?

